B.push(P(`Table 7 summarises the three confirmations, which span the range from success to complete failure. **Battery.** On measured battery degradation the model placed ${BW.IN} of ${BW.n} first warnings in the window (${f1(BW.pct)}%), with ${BW.late} late warnings, ${BW.missed} missed cell (the shortest-lived, ${BD.life_min} cycles) and none too early; all four hypotheses were supported. The warnings came a median of ${Math.round(BW.median_left_cycles)} cycles before failure, and the early limit could bind for ${f1(BW.early_limit_active_pct)}% of them. Age-only never warned for ${BAo.missed} of ${BAo.n} cells, because cell lives range from ${BD.life_min} to ${BD.life_max} cycles. Fig. 7a shows the capacity fade: slow at first, then a sharp knee, on which the warnings fall. Trained on two test batches and tested on the third, a harder secondary test, the model reached ${f1(BL.pct)}% (${BL.late} late), still above the MLP with Kalman filter (${f1(bd['lobo|mlp_kf|20'].pct)}%; Supplementary Section S5).`));
